WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.020
Dusk.

2
00:00:01.070 --> 00:00:02.760
A village church.

3
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:06.920
The bell hangs in its
tower, still and silent.

4
00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:11.790
Far away, smoke rises on the
horizon, with faint flashes.

5
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.340
Young men are dying out
there, far from home.

6
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:20.190
And the poem asks: "What candles
may be held to speed them all?"

7
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.180
These young men get no bells, no prayers,

8
00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:24.860
no proper funerals.

9
00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:26.870
So how are they mourned?

10
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.320
In this mission, you'll hear what takes
the place of each part of a funeral.

11
00:00:31.370 --> 00:00:35.530
You'll find the sonnet's turn, and
ask where its second half takes us.

12
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:39.540
And you'll pick apart the sounds
Owen builds out of gunfire.

13
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.090
Your mission: explain how
these dead are mourned.
